    {
      "page_title": "--target: Test Stage and CI Order",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What --target Does",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`--target s` builds up to and including stage ==s==",
            "One file can hold base, deps, dev, test, build, prod",
            "No `--target`: the **last** stage in the file is built"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Stage Graph",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "base",
              "deps",
              "build",
              "test",
              "prod"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`--target test` builds base, deps, build, test",
            "The `prod` stage is never built in that run"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. The Test Stage",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM build AS test",
            "RUN npm test"
          ],
          "note": "failing test fails docker build"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A failing `RUN npm test` stops the whole build",
            "Test stage never ships: prod does not copy from it",
            "Run it in CI before building the prod image"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. CI Order",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker build --target test .",
            "docker build --target prod \\",
            "  -t app:1.0 ."
          ],
          "note": "CI: test first, then ship prod"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`docker build --target test .` runs the tests",
            "On green, `docker build --target prod -t app:1.0 .`",
            "Cached layers from the test build are reused",
            "Push `app:1.0` to the registry"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Dev Stage and Compose",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "yaml",
          "lines": [
            "services:",
            "  web:",
            "    build:",
            "      context: .",
            "      target: dev"
          ],
          "note": "compose picks the stage per env"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "dev adds hot-reload tooling and ==devDependencies==",
            "`CMD [\"npm\",\"run\",\"dev\"]`, used with bind mounts",
            "BuildKit skips stages the target does not need"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Dev stage placed **last**: plain build ships dev tools",
            "Typo in `--target`: stage could not be found",
            "Test stage skipped in CI, so bad code reaches prod"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Keep prod last",
          "text": "A plain docker build then always makes the prod image."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Need files, not an image?",
          "text": "Use `--target export --output type=local,dest=./out`."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Why it works",
          "text": "Tests, dev tools and prod live in one file, and only the prod stage ships."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "one file, many images"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "ARG and ENV Across Stages",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What ARG and ENV Are",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==ARG== is a build-time variable: `--build-arg NAME=value`",
            "==ENV== persists into the running container too",
            "ARG before the first `FROM` is __global__, usable only in `FROM` lines",
            "ARG scope ends at the stage boundary"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. How Scope Works",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Declare `ARG` above the first `FROM`",
            "Use it in `FROM` lines: `golang:${GO_VERSION}`",
            "Inside a stage, redeclare: `ARG VERSION`",
            "No value given: it inherits the global default",
            "Each stage declares the ARGs it needs"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "ARG GO_VERSION=1.22",
            "ARG ALPINE_VERSION=3.20",
            "FROM golang:${GO_VERSION} AS build",
            "# redeclare to use it in this stage",
            "ARG GO_VERSION",
            "FROM alpine:${ALPINE_VERSION}"
          ],
          "note": "global ARG works only in FROM"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Value",
            "Crosses stages?",
            "Why"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "ARG",
              "No",
              "scope ends at FROM"
            ],
            [
              "ENV",
              "No",
              "fresh filesystem and config"
            ],
            [
              "ENV via FROM stage",
              "Yes",
              "child starts from parent"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Multi-Arch Builds",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Predefined ARG",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "BUILDPLATFORM",
              "machine running the build"
            ],
            [
              "TARGETPLATFORM",
              "platform of the image"
            ],
            [
              "TARGETOS",
              "target OS, e.g. linux"
            ],
            [
              "TARGETARCH",
              "target CPU, e.g. arm64"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM --platform=$BUILDPLATFORM \\",
            "  golang:1.22 AS build",
            "ARG TARGETOS",
            "ARG TARGETARCH",
            "RUN GOOS=$TARGETOS \\",
            "  GOARCH=$TARGETARCH go build"
          ],
          "note": "build natively, cross-compile out"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Cache and Runtime",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Changing an ARG invalidates ==later instructions== that use it",
            "Promote to runtime: `ENV APP_VERSION=$APP_VERSION`",
            "ARG alone vanishes once the container runs"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "FROM alpine:3.20",
            "ARG APP_VERSION=dev",
            "ENV APP_VERSION=$APP_VERSION",
            "CMD [\"env\"]"
          ],
          "note": "ENV keeps it at runtime"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Secrets",
          "text": "Use BuildKit secret mounts, not --build-arg, for tokens."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Build vs runtime"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Non-Root Users and Hardening",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Why Not Root",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Containers run as ==root== (UID 0) by default",
            "An escape or bug then has **maximum** privilege",
            "`USER` switches the user for later RUN, CMD, ENTRYPOINT"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Picking the User",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Base",
            "How to get a user"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "alpine",
              "`addgroup -S app && adduser -S -G app app`"
            ],
            [
              "debian",
              "`useradd -r app`"
            ],
            [
              "distroless",
              "`static:nonroot` = UID 65532"
            ],
            [
              "scratch",
              "hand-made `/etc/passwd` from builder"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerfile",
          "lines": [
            "RUN addgroup -S -g 10001 app \\",
            "&& adduser -S -u 10001 -G app app",
            "COPY --chown=app:app /out /app",
            "EXPOSE 8080",
            "USER 10001:10001"
          ],
          "note": "Numeric UID passes runAsNonRoot"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Why numeric?",
          "text": "Kubernetes runAsNonRoot cannot verify a name; a number it can."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Hardening Example",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Create the user in the ==build stage==",
            "`COPY --chown=app:app` keeps files readable",
            "Ports under 1024 need root: use **8080**, not 80",
            "Run with `docker run --read-only --tmpfs /tmp`"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Image",
            "HEALTHCHECK"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "alpine",
              "needs `curl` or a shell"
            ],
            [
              "distroless",
              "binary subcommand, no shell"
            ],
            [
              "scratch",
              "binary subcommand, no shell"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Verify the user",
          "text": "Run `docker run --rm app:1.0 id` and check the UID is not 0."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`USER` before `RUN apk add`: it fails, not root",
            "App dir owned by **root**: no logs or temp writes",
            "Port 80 as non-root: bind fails without capabilities",
            "Name-only `USER app` on Kubernetes checks"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Summary",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Rule",
          "text": "Install as root, then USER, own files, port 8080, read-only."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Numeric UID in `USER`",
            "`--chown` on every COPY",
            "Read-only root plus tmpfs"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Least privilege"
    },
    {
      "page_title": ".dockerignore and Cheatsheet",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What It Does",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==.dockerignore== lists paths kept out of the **build context** sent to the daemon",
            "Smaller context = faster builds, since less is uploaded",
            "Fewer accidental cache busts when irrelevant files change"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Template and Syntax",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerignore",
          "lines": [
            ".git",
            "node_modules",
            "dist",
            "coverage",
            "*.log",
            ".env"
          ],
          "note": "One pattern per line, relative to context"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "dockerignore",
          "lines": [
            "Dockerfile",
            "docker-compose.yml",
            "**/*.md",
            "!README.md"
          ],
          "note": "Last matching rule wins"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Pattern",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`*.log`",
              "logs in context root"
            ],
            [
              "`**/*.log`",
              "logs at any depth"
            ],
            [
              "`!README.md`",
              "re-include an exception"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "# beside Dockerfile.prod:",
            "Dockerfile.prod.dockerignore",
            "docker build -f Dockerfile.prod ."
          ],
          "note": "BuildKit only; wins over .dockerignore"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "No ignore file: `COPY . .` copies the host **node_modules** over the container's, breaking native modules",
            "Leaving `.env` and credentials in: secrets land in the **COPY layer**",
            "Ignoring a file your Dockerfile `COPY`s gives ==file not found==",
            "Fix: delete the pattern or add `!path` to re-include"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Summary and Checklist",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Build fat, ship thin",
          "text": "Keep toolchains in builder stages; copy only artifacts into a small **non-root** final image."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pin base tags or digests",
            "Order layers by change rate",
            "Use cache mounts",
            "Minimal final base"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Run as non-root",
            "Add a `.dockerignore`",
            "Test stage in CI"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Cheatsheet",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Need",
            "Syntax"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Name a stage",
              "`FROM x AS s`"
            ],
            [
              "Copy artifact",
              "`COPY --from=s`"
            ],
            [
              "Build to stage",
              "`--target s`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Need",
            "Syntax"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Cache dir",
              "`RUN --mount=type=cache`"
            ],
            [
              "Reuse ARG",
              "`ARG` redeclare"
            ],
            [
              "Drop root",
              "`USER nonroot`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
